 ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::START PARAM PRTCORD OUTPUT FROM SUBROUTINE CORD_PROC:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::

 ***********************************************************************************************************************************
                                                          P H A S E    1
                                                          --------------

 Phase 1: For CORD1R: (1) Change grid numbers (that were put into array CORD when B.D. was read) to the reference coordinate system
                          number for that grid.
                      (2) Put coords of the reference grids on the CORD1R into array RCORD.


 ***********************************************************************************************************************************
                                                          P H A S E    2
                                                          --------------

 Phase 2: Change coords on cylindrical and spherical systems to coords in terms of the defining rectangular axes of that system


 Array RCORD (cols 1-3) with coords of the 3 reference points in terms of the defining rectangular axes of the reference system
 -----------

     For CORD2C system       25 the location of pt A is:  0.000000E+00  0.000000E+00  0.000000E+00 in reference system        0
                                                   B is:  0.000000E+00  0.000000E+00  1.000000E+00 in reference system        0
                                                   C is:  1.000000E+00  0.000000E+00  0.000000E+00 in reference system        0


 ***********************************************************************************************************************************
                                                          P H A S E    3
                                                          --------------

 Phase 3: Check coordinate system data for logic:
          (1) There must be a final reference to the basic system (0)
          (2) There can be no circular references (i.e. a coord system can reference any number of other coord sys but cannot
              reference itself in that chain of refs).
          (3) Create RID_ARRAY which shows the chain of references of each coord system


 Trace of coordinate chain of references to basic system:
 --------------------------------------------------------


   References for coordinate system number       25
   ------------------------------------------------
     Coordinate system       25 references coordinate system        0


   RID_ARRAY: The cols below show the trace of a coord sys (number CID) through it's reference systems (RID's in the cols below CID)
   ---------  to the basic system (0). ICID is the internal coord system ID for actual coord system CID. Each CORD1C,R,S system will
              have 3 cols (one for each reference point on the CORD1C,R,S BDF entry). Only 1 col for each CID will be used in
              cascading the RID's back to CID to get the coord trnasformations from basic to CID.

     CID     ->       25
     RID   1 ->        0

 ***********************************************************************************************************************************
                                                          P H A S E    4
                                                          --------------

 Phase 4: Solve for array CASCADE_PROC_ARRAY. It will be used to do the cascading of coord references to get the transformation from
         CID to basic


   CASCADE_PROC_ARRAY array: (info from above RID_ARRAY used in the cascading of RID's from CID to basic(0))
   -------------------
     ICID          1
     Type     CORD2C
            --------
     Row 1:       25
     Row 2:        1
     Row 3:        1

     Row 1 of CASCADE_PROC_ARRAY is the CID coord sys number from RID_ARRAY
     Row 2 of CASCADE_PROC_ARRAY is the col number in RID_ARRAY to use when solving for the coord transformation from basic to CID
     Row 3 of CASCADE_PROC_ARRAY is the num of coord system refs above the basic sys (0) in RID_ARRAY (cascade from basic up to CID)

 ***********************************************************************************************************************************
                                                          P H A S E    5
                                                          --------------

 Phase 5: Get the unit vectors in each of the CORD2 coord systems in terms of their reference system. Put the results into array
          RCORD where the transformation matrices go. These are NOT the final transformations; they are the transformations from a
          CID to its reference system and ONLY for CORD2 systems (CORD1 systams will be handled later).


 RCORD array with data for a coord system relative to it's reference system. (only for CORD2 systems at this point)
 -----------

   RCORD array for coordinate system CID =        25 with values relative to it's reference coordiate system (RID) =         0
   -----------
     Cols  1- 3:  0.000000E+00 0.000000E+00 0.000000E+00: Origin of coord system       25 as measured in coord system        0

     Cols  4- 6:  1.000000E+00 0.000000E+00 0.000000E+00: Row 1 of matrix that transforms a vector to         0 from        25
     Cols  7- 9:  0.000000E+00 1.000000E+00 0.000000E+00: Row 2 of matrix that transforms a vector to         0 from        25
     Cols 10-12:  0.000000E+00 0.000000E+00 1.000000E+00: Row 3 of matrix that transforms a vector to         0 from        25

 ***********************************************************************************************************************************
                                                          P H A S E    6
                                                          --------------

 Phase 6:  Calculate transformations to basic (zero ) system for all CORD2 coordinate systems.


 RCORD array with data for a coord system relative to the basic system. (only for CORD2 systems at this point)
 -----------

   RCORD array for coordinate system CID =        25 with values relative to the basic system (RID) =         0
   -----------
     Cols  1- 3:  0.000000E+00 0.000000E+00 0.000000E+00: Origin of coord system       25 as measured in coord system        0

     Cols  4- 6:  1.000000E+00 0.000000E+00 0.000000E+00: Row 1 of matrix that transforms a vector to         0 from        25
     Cols  7- 9:  0.000000E+00 1.000000E+00 0.000000E+00: Row 2 of matrix that transforms a vector to         0 from        25
     Cols 10-12:  0.000000E+00 0.000000E+00 1.000000E+00: Row 3 of matrix that transforms a vector to         0 from        25


   Test to see which coordinate transformation matrices have been cascaded back to basic (0) coord system
   ----
   Coordinate system type         :   CORD2C
   Coordinate system ID           :       25
   Is transformation to basic done?        Y


 ***********************************************************************************************************************************
                                                          P H A S E    7
                                                          --------------

 Phase 7: Process CORD1 entries to get transformations to basic and put results into array RCORD


 ***********************************************************************************************************************************
                                                          P H A S E    8
                                                          --------------

 Phase 8: Check that all systems have been transformed to basic and rewrite RID's in array CORD to reflect this


 Test to see which coordinate transformation matrices have been cascaded back to basic (0) coord system
 ----
   Coordinate system type         :   CORD2C
   Coordinate system ID           :       25
   Is transformation to basic done?        Y


